{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Behavioral AML GNN (PayPal Topology)\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook demonstrates the **Behavioral GNN** approach designed for environments where counterparty information is missing (e.g., all transactions are to/from PayPal).\n",
    "\n",
    "Instead of linking Customers to Counterparties, we link them to **Behavioral Nodes**:\n",
    "- **Day of Week** (Synchronized schedules)\n",
    "- **Amount Buckets** (Structuring/Smurfing patterns)\n",
    "- **Bank Entity** (Institution targeting)\n",
    "- **Date Window** (Near-miss synchronization)\n",
    "\n",
    "This creates a graph where \"similarity of action\" becomes \"connectivity\"."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sys\n",
    "import os\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "\n",
    "# Add src to path\n",
    "sys.path.append(os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.getcwd(), '..')))\n",
    "\n",
    "from src.gnn.modeling.behavior_gnn import BehaviorGraphBuilder, BehavioralGNN, train_behavior_gnn, detect_behavioral_anomalies\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Modules loaded.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Generate \"Smurfing\" Mock Data\n",
    "\n",
    "We simulate a group of 10 Mules who all transact on **Fridays** (or adjacent days) with amounts between **$9,000 - $9,900**."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "np.random.seed(42)\n",
    "n_normal = 500\n",
    "n_mule = 20\n",
    "\n",
    "# 1. Normal Data (Random days, Random amounts)\n",
    "dates_normal = pd.date_range('2024-01-01', periods=n_normal*24, freq='H')\n",
    "df_normal = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'cust_id': [f'User_{{i}}' for i in range(n_normal)],\n",
    "    'amount': np.random.exponential(1000, n_normal),\n",
    "    'date': np.random.choice(dates_normal, n_normal),\n",
    "    'bank': np.random.choice(['Chase', 'Wells', 'BoA', 'Citi'], n_normal),\n",
    "    'type': 'Normal'\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "# 2. Mule Data (Synchronized on Fridays, Structuring amounts)\n",
    "# Friday Jan 5th, but let's say some hit Jan 6th (Saturday) too -> The Date Window helps here.\n",
    "fridays_fuzzy = ['2024-01-05', '2024-01-06', '2024-01-12', '2024-01-13']\n",
    "df_mule = pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    'cust_id': [f'Mule_{{i}}' for i in range(n_mule)],\n",
    "    'amount': np.random.uniform(9000, 9900, n_mule), # Structuring\n",
    "    'date': np.random.choice(fridays_fuzzy, n_mule), # Synchronized Day\n",
    "    'bank': 'SketchyCreditUnion',                    # Targeted Bank\n",
    "    'type': 'Mule'\n",
    "})\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.concat([df_normal, df_mule]).sample(frac=1).reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    "print(f\"Data Generated: {len(df)} txns. {n_mule} are Mules.\")\n",
    "df.tail()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Build Behavioral Graph (With Config)\n",
    "\n",
    "We define custom amount bins (to catch the $9k structuring) and a date window (to catch the Fri/Sat drift)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "config = {\n",
    "    'customer': 'cust_id',\n",
    "    'amount': 'amount',\n",
    "    'date': 'date',\n",
    "    'bank': 'bank',\n",
    "    \n",
    "    # Advanced Configuration\n",
    "    'date_window': 1, # Connect to T-1, T, T+1. Catch Fri/Sat sync.\n",
    "    'amount_bins': [-1, 1000, 5000, 9000, 10000, float('inf')] # Explicit structuring bin\n",
    "}\n",
    "\n",
    "builder = BehaviorGraphBuilder(config)\n",
    "data = builder.build(df)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Graph Structure:\")\n",
    "print(data)\n",
    "print(\"\\nNode Types:", data.node_types)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Train GNN\n",
    "\n",
    "The model learns that Mules are \"structurally similar\" because they share neighbors."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "model = BehavioralGNN(data.metadata(), hidden_channels=32, out_channels=32)\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Training...\")\n",
    "model = train_behavior_gnn(model, data, epochs=20, lr=0.01)\n",
    "print(\"Done.\")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Anomaly Detection\n",
    "\n",
    "Isolate the Mules."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "results = detect_behavioral_anomalies(model, data, builder.cust_map)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Merge back with ground truth labels for checking\n",
    "ground_truth = df[['cust_id', 'type']].drop_duplicates()\n",
    "merged = results.merge(ground_truth, left_on='customer_id', right_on='cust_id')\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Top 20 Highest Risk Customers:\")\n",
    "merged.sort_values('risk_score', ascending=False).head(20)"
   ]
  }
 ],
